We go into Nele's kitchen together.
The room is very bright and welcoming.
It already smells wonderful in here.
Nele is still cooking the main course.
She stands at the stove and stirs the food.
"I hope that you are very hungry," she says and laughs.
I answer her that I am really hungry.
Then I ask, "Can I help you?"
Nele nods gratefully.
"Yes, very gladly."
"We will eat soon," she says.
"Here is a cutting board."
She fetches the board and a sharp knife.
Then she gives me fresh herbs.
"I will chop them right away," I say.
I wash my hands and take the knife.
The fresh herbs smell glorious.
While I chop, we talk about the food.
Nele explains to me that the recipe is from her grandma.
I am sure that it will taste fantastic.
